# Line-ending policy for the repo root.
#
# Blobs are stored LF (they already are - this pins it rather than changing it);
# the working tree gets CRLF, matching the project preference in CLAUDE.md. That
# combination makes EOL-only differences stop showing as modified files, which is
# the same trick app/seed/*/.gitattributes already uses for markdown/canvas
# (Obsidian writes CRLF, the container writes LF).
#
# The exceptions below matter more than the default: they are the files that are
# read by Linux tooling, where a stray CR is not cosmetic but fatal.

* text=auto eol=crlf

# --- Must be LF -------------------------------------------------------------

# Shell scripts run in WSL and inside the containers. With a shebang, a CR makes
# the kernel look for an interpreter literally named "bash\r":
#   /usr/bin/env: 'bash\r': No such file or directory
# Without a shebang the failure is quieter and worse - the script runs, but every
# argument carries a trailing CR (docker-compose kill $'tzaraserver\r'), so
# commands fail against service names that look correct on screen.
# This has already bitten refresh-docs.sh, rebuild.sh and screenshot.sh.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Copied to .env by setup.sh/setup.ps1 and then parsed by compose's env_file and
# by shell `cut`/`sed` readers. Keep it LF so no value can pick up a trailing CR
# (POSTGRES_PASSWORD in particular is baked into the Postgres volume on first
# init and can never be corrected afterward).
.env.template text eol=lf

# --- Windows-native: CRLF is correct ----------------------------------------
# Redundant given the default above, but stated so the intent survives any later
# change to that default.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# --- Never transform --------------------------------------------------------
# `text=auto` already detects these by content; listed explicitly so a future
# blanket rule cannot corrupt them.
*.png  binary
*.ico  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf  binary
*.otf  binary
